// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Hamidon1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1108870646" "Hamidon's Monsters"
// DetailString :
"P3061834131" "You found a file that gives a brief overview on Hamidon's monsters. It seems they roam the wild, destroying anything in their path. One of the more important notes here is that they appear to be organic beings. The file ends by saying that the best weapon to 'clean them up' would be one that can eliminate purely organic life without damaging any structures."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Hamidon2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1816979744" "Hamidon's Power"
// DetailString :
"P1387471432" "This file is an attempt at documenting Hamidon's power. It seems Cole's regime is still investigating ways to destroy the Hamidon, should worse come to worse. The file details past attempts to destroy Hamidon. During the war, some nations resorted to nuclear strikes on their own cities in an attempt to stop the Hamidon. This worked, partially, but at a great cost. The note at the end says that a new solution would be one that, 'would not result in the destruction of man's home'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Hamidon3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2867256992" "Hamidon's Reach"
// DetailString :
"P2668009597" "Sewer Smasher had this torn up dossier on Hamidon. Most of the information can't be read anymore, save for one small sentence.<br><br>'Sometimes, when I look out to the forest, I can see it. I can only hope the production is done in time.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BAFEntrance 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P875287565" "Behavioral Adjustment Facility"
// DetailString :
"P2344564127" "You've found information regarding the Behavioral Adjustment Facility - the 'BAF'- in Imperial City. The main point of interest are blueprints of the facility, showing all the various nooks and crannies that can be seen. In the right hands, someone could easily use this to find ways to infiltrate the fortress."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - BeholderStorySouvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3538729898" "Seer Visor"
// tDetailString :
"P426435692" "Beholder gave you this Seer Visor from one of the seers you kidnapped. It reminds you of an experience you call...<br><br><color Paragon>Power of the Mind</color><br><br>It began with you helping Beholder, a former seer, capture four seers for a plan: to re-wire them as psychic bombs and to broadcast whatever messages the Resistance wanted to send all throughout Praetoria. It was easy enough to capture the seers, though you had to endure Mother Mayhem's voice taunting you while you were doing so.<br><br>You had some time to kill while Beholder was re-wiring the seers, so you went to recover information on Hamidon for Wardog. Beholder told you the information you found was apparently valuable, though Wardog refused to explain what it was for.<br><br>There was no time to wonder about this, however. Beholder had an issue: there was an aspect of Praetor Tilman controlling one of the seer's minds. You were sent into the woman's mind and destroyed Tilman's presence, freeing the seer from her influence.<br><br>Beholder activated the seers, unleashing their psychic blasts onto a specific PPD office, instantly killing everyone inside. You went in after the slaughter to collect information, only to run into what appeared to be sentient Clockwork who were looking for a woman named Penelope. You destroyed the Clockwork and found the information you needed: blueprints on the Behavioral Adjustment Facility in Imperial City.<br><br>Beholder told you that Vagabond had tremendous plans for these, but that she was done with being involved in the action. Everything that you did with her had tired her out; she claims she only has a few weeks left to live now and that she intends to live it out by watching the suffering of all those who are against the Resistance."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1223272827" "I believe in laying all the cards on the table from the very start, {HeroName}. That makes things faster for everyone. So pay attention, I'm only saying this once. Wardog is planning something very big. To start, he requires four seers. You see, {HeroName}, seers have the ability to put images directly into minds - a trick that Mother 'taught' all of us. We're going to kidnap seers to act as 'cameras', you could say, for our big event. But these seers will not simply be used as cameras. No, {HeroName}, these seers are going to be transformed into <color yellow>psychic bombs</color>. <br><br>I will re-program their minds to unleash immense psychic shockwaves. It will damage their minds beyond repair, but does it matter, really? Take it from me, Mother has seen to it that their minds are already dead. We're simply putting them to better use."
// AcceptString :
"P1715343853" "Sounds ambitious. What's the first step of this plan?"
// SendOffString :
"P3524353994" "The first step is retrieving those sisters... those seers who will act as our bombs. This is the benefit of working with me, {HeroName}. My broken, shattered life as a seer has allowed me access to all the secrets that the program has. I can direct you to one of the facilities where seers are commonly kept. That is where our four candidates are. Kidnap them and I will get to work reprogramming their minds. Just be careful. Mother tends to watch over her flock very closely. She may try to probe your mind. Do not worry. <color yellow>Vanessa DeVore</color> and I will keep you protected.<br><br>You had better hope that I don't die, however. My time is coming soon; whether it's in one minute or one month is anyone's guess."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2187824946" "Recover Seers for Beholder"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3056951699" "Let's not make a habit talking to each other like this, {HeroName}. If I'm going to die at any second, I don't want it to be while talking to you when you should be getting this done."
// TaskTitle :
"P877394765" "<color deepskyblue>Power of the Mind</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P4047529124" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Sisters</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2140462679" "You can feel something... strange in the air. As if someone is watching over this place very closely."

